{
  "about": "6 s pixel-stickman fight test (pixel6.py). Frames are STORY frames at 60 fps; figures are drawn on 1s at 30 fps (one drawing per 2 story frames, each held for 2 output frames at 60 fps). 'hitstop' counts extra 30 fps drawings frozen on the contact. Each contact frame is re-found from the attacker's effector speed (full extension after the speed peak) and the defender's reaction starts on it. 'at' places the move's key frame when align='key'. Moves: shared/assets/mocapmoves.",
  "fps": 60,
  "fight_drawings": 144,
  "fight_story_frames": 258,
  "transition_frames": 72,
  "crossfade": 6,
